# Code ownership — enforces the human review gate from CLAUDE.md §2.
#
# Anything touching auth, assessment, eiv or certificates requires human review
# before merge. A wrong result in those four areas is a compliance incident, not
# a bug, so the gate is mechanical rather than a convention someone remembers.
#
# Requires "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch.

# Default: everything is reviewed.
*                                       @masoudtahmasebi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The four compliance-critical areas. Never self-merge these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The pure core decides whether a physician earns a CME point.
/packages/domain/                       @masoudtahmasebi

# Auth is the trust anchor for the whole system (ADR-0003).
/apps/api/src/auth/                     @masoudtahmasebi

# Tenant isolation (ADR-0002) — a leak here is a reportable data incident.
/apps/api/src/db/                       @masoudtahmasebi
/db/migrations/                         @masoudtahmasebi
/infra/postgres/                        @masoudtahmasebi

# Assessment, EIV and certificates.
/apps/api/src/modules/assessment/       @masoudtahmasebi
/apps/api/src/modules/eiv/              @masoudtahmasebi
/apps/api/src/modules/certificate/      @masoudtahmasebi
/apps/eiv-harness/                      @masoudtahmasebi

